NNAAMMEE
     vviioorrnndd — VirtIO random number device

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     vviioorrnndd** aatt vviirrttiioo?? ffllaaggss 00xx0000

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The vviioorrnndd driver provides a virtual random number generator using a
     virtio(4) entropy device provided by QEMU 1.3 and later, and possibly by
     other hypervisors.

     As there is currently no way for vviioorrnndd to determine how much entropy is
     needed, the second byte of the flags value can be used to configure how
     often it should request more entropy from the host.  If the second lowest
     byte of the flags has a value from 1 to 15, vviioorrnndd will ask for 16 bytes
     of entropy every 15 * (1 << value) seconds.  For example, flags == 0x100
     means an interval of 30 seconds, 0x500 means 8 minutes, 0xa00 means 256
     minutes, and 0xf00 means about 6 days.  For flags == 0, a default value
     will be used (currently 8 minutes).  If the bit 0x1000 is set in the
     flags, vviioorrnndd will only request entropy from the host once during system
     boot.

